All done. Here's what was created:

**`configuration.go`** — the package with `Source`, `Config`, and `Load`:
- Defaults: `Port=8080`, `Name="helios"`, `Debug=false`
- Parses `HELIOS_PORT` via `strconv.Atoi`, validates range 1–65535
- Parses `HELIOS_NAME` as a non-empty string; present-but-empty is an error
- Parses `HELIOS_DEBUG` via `strconv.ParseBool`
- Parse errors are wrapped with `%w` so callers can reach `*strconv.NumError` via `errors.As`

**`cmd/configprint/main.go`** — CLI that reads from `os.LookupEnv` and prints `port=N name=S debug=true|false`.

**`configuration_test.go`** — tests covering:
- Defaults when source returns nothing
- Valid port values including boundaries (1, 65535)
- Port errors: non-numeric, out of range (0, -1, 65536, 99999)
- Port parse error preserves `*strconv.NumError` wrapping
- Name override and empty-name error
- Debug parsing (true/false/1/0/T/F) and parse error wrapping
- Partial config (only one key set, others use defaults)

`go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `go test ./...` — all pass.
